# Line-ending and diff policy for the dissertation repo.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (added 2026-08-22, audit vi)
# -------------------------------------------------
# The repository had mixed line endings: the headline result tables and
# milestone notes were written CRLF, the `_hmm` comparator artefacts LF. The two
# sets are produced by the same code on the same machine, so the difference is
# an accident of when each file was last written -- but it means a re-run of any
# phase produces a diff full of whole-file line-ending churn, which hides the
# handful of lines that actually changed. That is a real risk for this project:
# every audit round so far has turned on noticing a small numeric change in a
# generated file.
#
# Policy: normalise every text file to LF in the index AND in the working tree.
# LF in the working tree (rather than CRLF-on-checkout) is deliberate -- the
# analysis reads these CSVs with pandas, which is agnostic, and a single ending
# everywhere means a file's stored form and its on-disk form always agree.
#
# ONE-TIME MIGRATION: after adding this file, run once
#     git add --renormalize .
# and commit the result as its own commit ("normalise line endings"), separate
# from any content change. That commit will touch many files and no content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Explicit binaries: never converted, never diffed as text ---------------
*.parquet   binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.pdf       binary
*.docx      binary
*.dotx      binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.zip       binary
*.pt        binary
*.pth       binary
*.pkl       binary
*.ckpt      binary

# --- Text, but with a declared ending ---------------------------------------
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.csv       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.ipynb     text eol=lf

# The Oxford-Man source CSV is a tracked data artefact, not source: keep it
# byte-for-byte as downloaded so its checksum stays meaningful.
Code/data/raw/oxfordman/** -text -diff
